    ERR_NONE                                       = 0;
    ERR_NOT_INITIALIZED                            = 1;
    ERR_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY                          = 2;
    ERR_NULL_PTR                                   = 3;
}; What would be a simple, maintainable (e.g., sed tends to be hard to decipher) way to alert me if a discrepancy occurs between the two? A discrepancy could be either differing order between elements or missing elements. As you can see, a simple call to "diff" won't make it since the proto file contains explicit values for the elements and does not have exactly the same syntax as C. I couldn't find existing tools for this purpose. Would a simple parsing approach be easier to maintain than a full fledged program such as a Python script which instantiate copies of the enums to compare them?

